{"uid":"modules/lazy_heat.py","name":"lazy_heat.py","qualname":"modules/lazy_heat.py","kind":"module","file":"modules/lazy_heat.py","line":1,"end_line":406,"language":"py","signature":"","params":[],"returns":"","decorators":[],"bases":[],"modifiers":[],"visibility":"public","doc":{"summary":"Heat tiers and version math for CVE correlation.","description":"Heat is a deterministic pre-classification of a CVE from its\nexploitation and severity signals so the pipeline can prioritise what\ncorrelators and the autonomous loop look at first:\n\n  hot   — actively dangerous now: KEV, public/weaponized exploit,\n          critical CVSS (>= 9.0), or high EPSS plus high CVSS\n  warm  — warning signs: high CVSS (>= 7.0) or EPSS threshold reached\n  cold  — low-priority watch: everything else\n\nA match's heat on *your* host differs from the feed heat: a match the\nhost's distribution already backported a fix for is cold however hot\nthe CVE is, and a confirmed match on a high score reads as hot.\n\nVersion helpers are pure stdlib so every rule is unit-testable without\nnetwork access. Thresholds live in one place and are easy to retune.\n\nStdlib only. Never raises on untrusted input; every entry point\ndegrades to \"unknown\" when data is missing.","params":[],"returns":null,"yields":null,"raises":[],"attributes":[],"examples":[],"notes":[],"see_also":[],"deprecated":"","since":"","style":"plain"},"parent":"","members":["modules/lazy_heat.py::HOT","modules/lazy_heat.py::WARM","modules/lazy_heat.py::COLD","modules/lazy_heat.py::HIGH_CVSS","modules/lazy_heat.py::CRITICAL_CVSS","modules/lazy_heat.py::EPSS_THRESHOLD","modules/lazy_heat.py::HEAT_RANK","modules/lazy_heat.py::SEVERITY_FROM_HEAT","modules/lazy_heat.py::SEVERITY_HEAT","modules/lazy_heat.py::PATCHED","modules/lazy_heat.py::VULNERABLE","modules/lazy_heat.py::UNKNOWN","modules/lazy_heat.py::NO_DATA","modules/lazy_heat.py::classify_heat","modules/lazy_heat.py::match_heat","modules/lazy_heat.py::parse_version","modules/lazy_heat.py::compare_versions","modules/lazy_heat.py::version_in_range","modules/lazy_heat.py::cvss3_base_score","modules/lazy_heat.py::product_token","modules/lazy_heat.py::token_matches","modules/lazy_heat.py::parse_distro_revision","modules/lazy_heat.py::backport_status","modules/lazy_heat.py::label_for"],"inferred_raises":[],"returns_value":null,"value":"","base_uids":[],"subclasses":[],"calls":[],"called_by":[]}
